      <h1><em>Classic Cocktails at Home: 5 Easy Recipes</em></h1>
      <p class="article-meta">By the Monarch Liquor team &middot; Updated Sept 2026</p>
    </header>

    <!-- Article Body -->
    <article class="content-section" style="padding-top: 20px;">
      <div class="content-narrow prose">
        <p>You don't need a speakeasy license or a drawer of weird bar tools to make a great drink. These five classics cover most occasions, and every ingredient is on our shelves. One shaker, one jigger, and you're in business.</p>

        <h2>1. Margarita</h2>
        <p>The Austin house cocktail. Skip the sour mix forever.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>2 oz blanco tequila</li>
          <li>1 oz fresh lime juice</li>
          <li>3/4 oz orange liqueur (Cointreau or Naranja)</li>
          <li>1/4 oz agave syrup (optional, to taste)</li>
          <li>Salt for the rim, lime wheel to garnish</li>
        </ul>
        <p><em>Shake everything with ice, strain over fresh ice in a salt-rimmed rocks glass.</em></p>

        <h2>2. Ranch Water</h2>
        <p>West Texas's gift to hot afternoons &mdash; basically a margarita's minimalist cousin.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>2 oz blanco tequila (or Desert Door sotol for the Texas power move)</li>
          <li>1/2 oz fresh lime juice</li>
          <li>Topo Chico, to top</li>
        </ul>
        <p><em>Build in a tall glass with ice, top with Topo Chico, stir once. Some folks just pour the tequila and lime straight into the Topo bottle &mdash; we don't judge.</em></p>

        <h2>3. Old Fashioned</h2>
        <p>The drink that made whiskey famous. Simple, but precision matters.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>2 oz bourbon or rye</li>
          <li>1/4 oz simple syrup (or 1 sugar cube)</li>
          <li>2&ndash;3 dashes Angostura bitters</li>
          <li>Orange peel to garnish</li>
        </ul>
        <p><em>Stir with ice for 20&ndash;30 seconds, strain over one big cube, express the orange peel over the top.</em> Need a bottle? Our <a href="/guides/best-bourbon-whiskey-austin.html">bourbon guide</a> has picks at every price.</p>

