        <h2>4. Paloma</h2>
        <p>Mexico's favorite tequila drink, and arguably better than the margarita for a crowd.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>2 oz blanco or reposado tequila</li>
          <li>1/2 oz fresh lime juice</li>
          <li>Grapefruit soda (Jarritos or Squirt), to top</li>
          <li>Pinch of salt, grapefruit wedge to garnish</li>
        </ul>
        <p><em>Build over ice in a tall glass, top with grapefruit soda, stir gently.</em> Shortcut: Deep Eddy Ruby Red vodka plus soda water gets you 90% of the way there &mdash; more Texas swaps in our <a href="/guides/texas-spirits-guide.html">Texas Spirits Guide</a>.</p>

        <h2>5. Espresso Martini</h2>
        <p>The dinner-party closer. Yes, it's back. No, it never really left.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>1.5 oz vodka</li>
          <li>1 oz coffee liqueur (Kahl&uacute;a or Mr Black)</li>
          <li>1 oz fresh espresso (or strong cold brew), cooled</li>
          <li>1/4 oz simple syrup, to taste</li>
          <li>3 coffee beans to garnish</li>
        </ul>
        <p><em>Shake hard with ice &mdash; harder than feels reasonable &mdash; and strain into a chilled coupe. The foam is the point.</em></p>

        <h2>Stocking a Starter Bar</h2>
        <p>If you're building from zero, this covers all five recipes: a blanco tequila, a bourbon, a vodka, orange and coffee liqueurs, Angostura bitters, agave or simple syrup, and a case of Topo Chico. Bring this list to either store (or order it all online) and you're one lime run away from a full home bar.</p>
